From: Gemtek W1700K tree <local>
Date: Fri, 1 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: switch HW GRO offload to NETIF_F_GRO_HW

Finish the migration of the airoha HW GRO/LRO offload (in-tree 916-02 +
920-1x reworks) to the net-next v3 form: advertise the offload as the
forwarding-safe NETIF_F_GRO_HW instead of NETIF_F_LRO (LRO is force-
disabled by the stack on bridged/routed ports), move the LRO-capable
rx-queue selection to the high queues (24-31), reject open on a shared
QDMA when this device already has HW GRO in its feature set, skip HW
programming while the netdev is down, and tighten the zero-payload
segment check. Equivalent to Lorenzo's v3 "add HW GRO offload support".

Signed-off-by: local <local>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
 
 #define AIROHA_LRO_PAGE_ORDER		order_base_2(SZ_16K / PAGE_SIZE)
 #define AIROHA_MAX_NUM_LRO_QUEUES	8
-#define AIROHA_RXQ_LRO_EN_MASK		GENMASK(7, 0)
+#define AIROHA_RXQ_LRO_EN_MASK		GENMASK(31, 24)
 #define AIROHA_RXQ_LRO_MAX_AGG_COUNT	64
 #define AIROHA_RXQ_LRO_MAX_AGG_TIME	100
 #define AIROHA_RXQ_LRO_MAX_AGE_TIME	2000
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -797,7 +797,7 @@
 		return NULL;
 
 	data_off = th_off + (th->doff << 2);
-	if (len < data_off)
+	if (len <= data_off)
 		return NULL;
 
 	tcp_win = FIELD_GET(QDMA_ETH_RXMSG_TCP_WIN_MASK, msg3);
@@ -2142,14 +2142,16 @@
 	u32 pse_port = FE_PSE_PORT_PPE1;
 	int err, qdma_id;
 
-	/* HW LRO is configured on the QDMA and it is shared between
+	/* HW GRO is configured on the QDMA and it is shared between
 	 * all the devices using it. Refuse to open a second device on
-	 * the same QDMA if LRO is enabled on any device sharing it.
+	 * the same QDMA if HW GRO is enabled on any device sharing it
+	 * or if this device has HW GRO enabled in its feature set.
 	 */
 	qdma = airoha_qdma_deref(dev);
 	qdma_id = qdma - &eth->qdma[0];
 
-	if (qdma->users && airoha_fe_lro_is_enabled(eth, qdma_id)) {
+	if (qdma->users && (airoha_fe_lro_is_enabled(eth, qdma_id) ||
+			    (netdev->features & NETIF_F_GRO_HW))) {
 		netdev_warn(netdev, "required to disable HW GRO on QDMA%d\n",
 			    qdma_id);
 		return -EBUSY;
@@ -2563,6 +2565,9 @@
 	if (!(diff & NETIF_F_GRO_HW))
 		return 0;
 
+	if (!netif_running(netdev))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (features & NETIF_F_GRO_HW)
 		airoha_dev_lro_enable(dev);
 	else
@@ -3904,7 +3909,7 @@
 	netdev->ethtool_ops = &airoha_ethtool_ops;
 	netdev->max_mtu = AIROHA_MAX_MTU;
 	netdev->watchdog_timeo = 5 * HZ;
-	netdev->hw_features = AIROHA_HW_FEATURES | NETIF_F_LRO;
+	netdev->hw_features = AIROHA_HW_FEATURES | NETIF_F_GRO_HW;
 	netdev->features |= AIROHA_HW_FEATURES;
 	netdev->vlan_features = AIROHA_HW_FEATURES;
 	SET_NETDEV_DEV(netdev, eth->dev);
